%% @fig 01
%% @kicker The four-phase agent loop
%% @alt The agent loop drawn as a circular track: perceive, think, act, and remember in sequence, returning to perceive until the task is complete or a stop condition ends the run. A task enters at perceive, the run exits from remember, and the context window at the centre fills as the loop repeats.
%% @caption Each phase has its own failure modes: infinite loops start in act, context exhaustion and lost tool results start in remember.
%% @ring perceive>think>act>remember | 128
%% @center tokens rows=3,5,7 scale=1.6
%% @glyph task | inbox
%% @glyph perceive | eye
%% @glyph think | core
%% @glyph act | tools
%% @glyph remember | cells fill=0.7 flag
%% @glyph done | stop
flowchart LR
  task["Task"]
  perceive["Perceive"]:::accent
  think["Think"]:::accent
  act["Act"]:::accent
  remember["Remember"]:::accent
  done["Done"]
  task --> perceive
  perceive --> think
  think --> act
  act --> remember
  remember --> perceive
  remember --> done
